# MINIATURE EXACT ORACLE — composition-correctness gate for the MSP pipeline
# (design-log §4.12, 2026-06-12). Generated by scripts/generate_miniature_oracle.py
# p=0.001; qubits: 0,1,2 = rep-code block, 3 = check/SE ancilla (morph wire),
# 4 = magic wire (later the second SE ancilla). 5 measurements, 2 deterministic
# detectors, 23 noise locations. Records: 0,1 = XS-checks (DETECTORs), 2 = teleport
# byproduct (the frame rule), 3,4 = noiseless end-SE syndrome (Z0Z1, Z1Z2).
# --- magic injection: T on |+>
RX 4
Z_ERROR(0.001) 4
T 4
DEPOLARIZE1(0.001) 4
TICK
# --- XS-check 1: controlled-(T X T_DAG) sandwich from a |+> ancilla
RX 3
Z_ERROR(0.001) 3
T 4
S_DAG 4
DEPOLARIZE1(0.001) 4
CX 3 4
DEPOLARIZE2(0.001) 3 4
T 4
DEPOLARIZE1(0.001) 4
Z_ERROR(0.001) 3
MX 3
DETECTOR rec[-1]
TICK
# --- XS-check 2: controlled-(T X T_DAG) sandwich from a |+> ancilla
RX 3
Z_ERROR(0.001) 3
T 4
S_DAG 4
DEPOLARIZE1(0.001) 4
CX 3 4
DEPOLARIZE2(0.001) 3 4
T 4
DEPOLARIZE1(0.001) 4
Z_ERROR(0.001) 3
MX 3
DETECTOR rec[-1]
TICK
# --- one-bit teleport: magic wire -> block root 0 (Z^m byproduct = frame rule);
# MX 4 is the abandoned-wire X-basis read
R 0
X_ERROR(0.001) 0
CX 4 0
DEPOLARIZE2(0.001) 4 0
Z_ERROR(0.001) 4
MX 4
TICK
# --- encode into the 3-qubit repetition code
R 1 2
X_ERROR(0.001) 1 2
CX 0 1
DEPOLARIZE2(0.001) 0 1
CX 0 2
DEPOLARIZE2(0.001) 0 2
DEPOLARIZE1(0.001) 0 1 2
TICK
# --- NOISELESS end-of-circuit SE of the rep code (Z0Z1, Z1Z2), wires 3,4 reused
R 3 4
CX 0 3 1 3
CX 1 4 2 4
M 3 4
DETECTOR(0, 0, 4) rec[-2]
DETECTOR(0, 0, 4) rec[-1]
# --- full k=1 equator Bloch decomposition of the teleported T|+>
PAULI_EXPECTATION(0) X0*X1*X2 rec[-3]
PAULI_EXPECTATION(1) Y0*X1*X2 rec[-3]
